{
  "$comment": [
    "Suites that cannot pass without a host capability. 'profiles' holds the shared",
    "explanation; 'entries' only name files and the profile they belong to.",
    "kind=environment entries are re-checked on every run: when the probes succeed the",
    "suite runs again with no edit, so a quarantine cannot hide a working test.",
    "alwaysSkip marks a capability that cannot be probed cheaply; reviewBy is then the",
    "only thing forcing a re-check.",
    "kind=fixture entries are real red tests: they stay skipped until someone fixes the",
    "cause, and reviewBy makes the entry fail the gate once it is overdue."
  ],
  "profiles": {
    "rpc-launch": {
      "kind": "environment",
      "probes": [
        "ps",
        "flock"
      ],
      "owner": "engine / RPC",
      "reviewBy": "2026-11-18",
      "reason": "These suites execute the real RPC launch wrapper, which takes the run lock with flock and proves the launch process is its own group leader with 'ps -o pgid='. A host without the flock binary (stock macOS) or without permission to call ps cannot run them. Verified on 2026-10-19: with flock/ps shims on PATH these suites pass, and the only one that still needs a real flock is engine-rpc-run-guard.test.ts, because it tests lock contention and TERM/KILL takeover."
    },
    "electron-sandbox": {
      "kind": "environment",
      "owner": "renderer / notebook",
      "reviewBy": "2026-11-18",
      "alwaysSkip": true,
      "reason": "The suite boots a real Electron BrowserWindow. Restricted runners reject it with 'sandbox initialization failed: Operation not permitted' before any assertion runs, so the failure says nothing about the editor code."
    },
    "real-ssh-server": {
      "kind": "environment",
      "owner": "engine / SSH",
      "reviewBy": "2026-11-18",
      "alwaysSkip": true,
      "reason": "The suite connects to a real OpenSSH server to exercise host-key trust. Without a reachable server it fails in under 200ms with RemoteSshConnectionError/network_unreachable, never reaching the assertion under test."
    },
    "pty": {
      "kind": "environment",
      "owner": "terminal / remote",
      "reviewBy": "2026-11-18",
      "alwaysSkip": true,
      "reason": "The suite allocates a real PTY through the terminal worker. Restricted runners reject it with 'failed to openpty: Operation not permitted' (EPERM) before the ssh argv and resize assertions run."
    },
    "concurrency-sensitive": {
      "kind": "environment",
      "owner": "wrappers / jobs",
      "reviewBy": "2026-11-01",
      "alwaysSkip": true,
      "reason": "Passes 26/26 when run alone (checked twice on 2026-10-19) but fails inside the full run at --test-concurrency=4 after ~19s, so the suite is not isolated from other suites' load. Re-run it alone before trusting a green gate; the real fix is test isolation, not a skip."
    }
  },
